  "live_records": {
    "q-341473": {
      "dom_id": "step-q341473",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "$$\n\nIf $y=\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡({x}^{2}+4)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+4),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+4}$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,[\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡({x}^{2}+4)-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+4)] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{|{x}^{2}+4|\\sqrt{1+{({x}^{2}+4)}^{2}}}\\cdot {({x}^{2}+4)}^{′}-\\frac{{({x}^{2}+4)}^{′}}{{x}^{2}+4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{({x}^{2}+4)\\sqrt{1+({x}^{4}+8{x}^{2}+16)}}\\cdot 2x-\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2x}{({x}^{2}+4)\\sqrt{{x}^{4}+8{x}^{2}+17}}-\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+4} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+4}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{4}+8{x}^{2}+17}}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
