    "q-341483": {
      "dom_id": "step-q341483",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "$$\n\nIf $y=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡({sin}^{2}⁡x),$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\,[\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡({sin}^{2}⁡x)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot [-\\frac{1}{|{sin}^{2}⁡x|\\sqrt{1+{({sin}^{2}⁡x)}^{2}}}]\\cdot {({sin}^{2}⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2{sin}^{2}⁡x\\sqrt{1+{sin}^{4}⁡x}}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+{sin}^{4}⁡x}}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}⁡x}{\\sqrt{1+{sin}^{4}⁡x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
