    "q-95513": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95513",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "$$\n\nIf $y=3\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡\\sqrt{x},$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosecant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcsch}⁡\\sqrt{x}) \\\\  & =-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{|\\sqrt{x}|\\sqrt{1+{(\\sqrt{x})}^{2}}}\\cdot (\\sqrt{x})^{′} \\\\  & =-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}\\cdot \\sqrt{1+x}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2x\\sqrt{1+x}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
