    "q-95522": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95522",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "$$\n\nIf $y=-\\operatorname{arsech}⁡5x,$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic secant function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡x)=-\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-\\operatorname{arsech}⁡5x) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsech}⁡5x) \\\\  & =-(-\\frac{1}{(5x)\\sqrt{1-(5x)^{2}}})\\cdot (5x)^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5x\\sqrt{1-25{x}^{2}}}\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{x\\sqrt{1-25{x}^{2}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-95522-a",
